A good way to make this round-trip lossless is:

- keep the current behavior by default
- add an opt-in “lossless” mode
- in that mode, encode only the ambiguous kebab segments in a way that is still readable in camelCase and reversible in both directions

## Core idea

Normal kebab/camel transforms lose information because camelCase has no natural separator for:

- digit-starting segments: `grid-2x2` → `grid2x2`
- single-letter segments: `a-z` → `aZ`
- acronym-like runs created from multiple short segments: `arrow-down-a-z` → `arrowDownAZ`

So in lossless mode, make those ambiguous segment boundaries explicit in camelCase with a reserved marker.

A practical choice is `_`.

### Encoding rule

When converting from kebab to camel in lossless mode:

- normal segments behave as usual
- but if a segment is “ambiguous”, prefix its camel contribution with `_`

Ambiguous segment types:

1. segment starts with a digit  
   `2x2` → `_2x2`

2. segment is a single character  
   `a` → `_A` when non-initial  
   `z` → `_Z`

That gives:

- `grid-2x2` → `grid_2x2`
- `heading-1` → `heading_1`
- `arrow-down-a-z` → `arrowDown_A_Z`
- `a-large-small` → `aLargeSmall` if leading `a` is first segment and left alone
- `a-z` → `a_Z`

When converting from camel to kebab in lossless mode:

- `_` marks the start of an original kebab segment
- uppercase still marks normal camel word boundaries

So:

- `grid_2x2` → `grid-2x2`
- `heading_1` → `heading-1`
- `arrowDown_A_Z` → `arrow-down-a-z`

This preserves both round-trips.

---

# Why this works well for web components

It matches your ergonomics goals pretty well:

- attributes remain very natural:
  - `inner-html`
  - `grid-2x2`
  - `arrow-down-a-z`
- properties remain readable and inferable:
  - `innerHtml`
  - `grid_2x2`
  - `arrowDown_A_Z`

That is much better than intrusive escaping in HTML like `inner-h-t-m-l`, and also much better than opaque escape tokens.

The compromise is:

- ordinary names stay ordinary
- only edge-case names get underscores in the property form

That fits the “one side is source of truth, the other is acceptable and understandable” goal.

---

# Proposed API

```js
kebabToCamel(str, { lossless: true })
camelToKebab(str, { lossless: true })
```

Default remains unchanged when `lossless` is absent or false.

---

# Reference implementation

```js
function kebabToCamel(str, options = {}) {
  if (!options.lossless) {
    return str.replace(/-([a-zA-Z0-9])/g, (_, ch) => ch.toUpperCase());
  }

  const parts = str.split('-');
  if (parts.length === 0) return str;

  return parts
    .map((part, index) => {
      if (index === 0) return part;

      const ambiguous =
        part.length === 1 || /^[0-9]/.test(part);

      if (ambiguous) {
        if (part.length === 1) {
          return '_' + part.toUpperCase();
        }
        return '_' + part;
      }

      return part[0].toUpperCase() + part.slice(1);
    })
    .join('');
}

function camelToKebab(str, options = {}) {
  if (!options.lossless) {
    return str.replace(/([a-z0-9])([A-Z])/g, '$1-$2').toLowerCase();
  }

  let out = '';
  let i = 0;

  while (i < str.length) {
    const ch = str[i];

    if (ch === '_') {
      if (out && out[out.length - 1] !== '-') out += '-';
      i++;

      if (i < str.length) {
        out += str[i].toLowerCase();
        i++;
        while (i < str.length && /[a-zA-Z0-9]/.test(str[i]) && str[i] !== '_') {
          const next = str[i];
          if (/[A-Z]/.test(next)) {
            break;
          }
          out += next.toLowerCase();
          i++;
        }
      }
      continue;
    }

    if (/[A-Z]/.test(ch)) {
      if (out && out[out.length - 1] !== '-') out += '-';
      out += ch.toLowerCase();
      i++;
      continue;
    }

    out += ch;
    i++;
  }

  return out;
}
```

---

# Simpler and more robust implementation

The `camelToKebab` parser can be made cleaner by tokenizing:

```js
function kebabToCamel(str, options = {}) {
  if (!options.lossless) {
    return str.replace(/-([a-zA-Z0-9])/g, (_, ch) => ch.toUpperCase());
  }

  const parts = str.split('-');

  return parts.map((part, i) => {
    if (i === 0) return part;

    if (part.length === 1) return '_' + part.toUpperCase();
    if (/^\d/.test(part)) return '_' + part;

    return part[0].toUpperCase() + part.slice(1);
  }).join('');
}

function camelToKebab(str, options = {}) {
  if (!options.lossless) {
    return str.replace(/([a-z0-9])([A-Z])/g, '$1-$2').toLowerCase();
  }

  let result = '';
  let i = 0;

  while (i < str.length) {
    const ch = str[i];

    if (ch === '_') {
      if (result) result += '-';
      i++;

      if (i >= str.length) break;

      if (/[A-Z]/.test(str[i])) {
        result += str[i].toLowerCase();
        i++;
      } else {
        while (i < str.length && /[a-z0-9]/i.test(str[i]) && str[i] !== '_') {
          result += str[i].toLowerCase();
          i++;
        }
      }
      continue;
    }

    if (/[A-Z]/.test(ch)) {
      if (result) result += '-';
      result += ch.toLowerCase();
    } else {
      result += ch;
    }

    i++;
  }

  return result;
}
```

